<title>INDIA: India's Apr 96-Jan 97 trade deficit at 4.3 bln.</title>
<headline>India's Apr 96-Jan 97 trade deficit at 4.3 bln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's trade deficit rose to $4.29 billion betwen April 1996 to January 1997, compared with $4.06 billion in the same period a year earlier, the government said on Friday.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Apr-Jan 96/97    Apr-Mar 95/96</p>
<p>    Exports		     27.06		25.49</p>
<p>    Imports		     31.35		29.54</p>
<p>    Trade balance	     -4.29		-4.06</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.  </p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports increased to $2.84 billion in January, up 8.77 percent from $2.61 billion in the same month in 1996, the government said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.84	2.75	 2.61</p>
<p>    Imports		  3.75	3.14	 3.06</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.91     -0.39	-0.45</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
</text>
